{"type":"result","arm":"DNSALT","kind":"dns","label":"selftest","parameters":{"seconds":8,"ratePerSecond":50,"tcpPercent":20,"cnameEvery":0,"dnsPort":5302,"drainWindowMs":1000},"metrics":{"sent":402,"udpSent":321,"tcpSent":81,"unsent":0,"udpUnsent":0,"tcpUnsent":0,"offered":402,"answered":402,"servfail":0,"timeout":0,"other":0,"unanswered":0,"socketErrors":0,"emptyAnswers":70,"malformed":0,"unmatched":0,"answerRate":1,"achievedRate":50.236,"rcodes":{"0":402},"queryTypes":{"A":236,"TXT":6,"AAAA":96,"HTTPS":64}},"latency":{"dns-rtt":{"count":402,"minUs":393.074,"maxUs":1904.428,"meanUs":557.802,"p50Us":547.583,"p90Us":625.663,"p99Us":724.735,"p999Us":1904.639}},"gates":{"clientSendLoss":0,"windowMs":0},"notes":["every query written to the socket is terminal in exactly one of answered (rcode 0), servfail (rcode != 0), timeout (still unmatched when the drain window closed) or other (tcp only: a response consumed a queued query but carried a different transaction id); answered \u002B servfail \u002B timeout \u002B other == sent, and unanswered is timeout \u002B other.","drainWindowMs is not a per-query deadline. Once the send phase ends the arm keeps reading for that long and only then books every query still pending as timeout, so a query answered inside the window counts as answered however long it took, and a response that arrives after the window is closed can only be counted unmatched. cnameEvery \u003E 0 replaces every cnameEvery-th query with a CNAME query, and because the udp path is keyed by transaction id, a udp response whose id matches no outstanding query is unmatched and can never be other.","unsent counts pacing slots skipped because the in-flight window was full: those queries never reached the socket and are in no outcome, so offered is sent \u002B unsent and neither answerRate nor achievedRate includes them; socketErrors counts socket-level failures (connect, send, receive) that belong to no single query.","answerRate is answered / sent and achievedRate is sent per elapsed second; both divide the sent population, not the offered one.","queryTypes counts the queries actually written to the socket, per DNS type, so the mix is measured from QueryTypeFor rather than declared: a plan interleaving CNAME queries shows them here instead of hiding them.","transaction ids are reused on wraparound; a response matching no outstanding query is counted as unmatched, never as answered, and on TCP the response is matched against the id queued with the query it is credited to."],"startedTicks":19936297768885,"endedTicks":19944300139160}
